  "body": "**Blocked by:** #125\n\n## Context\n\nNative and MCP tools require one availability pipeline and the same absence-of-capability behavior.\n\n## Task\n\nAdapt active MCP registrations into ModuleRegistry's `agentTools` projection. For a project run, include exactly active-server and active-registration tools whose `project_mcp_grants.granted=true`. Extend generated permission facts with this fourth source. Tool schemas/descriptions come from the synchronized snapshot. A grant controls visibility only; retain `requiresApproval` and `riskClass` for per-invocation approval. Deactivation or grant revocation removes discovery and invocation immediately without deleting registration history.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Registry adapter, per-project intersection, manifest facts, and activation behavior.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Approval queue implementation and native core operation catalog.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Ungranted/inactive tools are absent and unknown on invocation.\n- Granted tools preserve approval metadata.\n- Two projects can expose different subsets of one server.\n",
